extends RefCounted

const SITE := "Briar Lane / temporary works office / 1998\n\nNos. 13–19 have been vacated for clearance. No. 17 is retained as the site office until the final inspection. Front room: waiting area. Rear room: property files.\n\nLeave the service feed connected until the last worker has signed out. Check the electrical occupancy counter against the handwritten register. The counter alone is not proof that a building is empty.\n\nAfter the final close-out, remove the address from the call-out list.\n\nA pencil note at the bottom: Counter has shown two all night. Only one contractor checked in."

const CALL := "Work Order 017 / 17 Briar Lane\nEli Ward / night call-out\n\nCaller reports a television playing inside an empty property. The service list says the supply is disconnected. No owner contact. Caller withheld.\n\nThe address was removed from the list in 1999. Dispatch almost cancelled the job.\n\nThen they read out the address. I've kept Dad's last work slip since I was seven. Seventeen Briar Lane. He never came home from this job. I asked them to leave it with me."
const ARCHIVE := "Property file / Simon Ward / electrician / 1998\n\nArrival entered at 23:17. No departure entered. At 23:18 his name was changed to ABSENT. The door log shows no movement.\n\nAttached missing-person report: Simon did not return from the call. His son Eli was seven.\n\nThere is a second man in the service-camera still. No name, no vehicle entry. Dad wrote beside it: He was at the stairs when I tried to leave.\n\nDad asked for his original field return to be kept. It was never collected. A brass service key is clipped inside the file."
const PROCEDURE := "Dad's service notes / 1998\n\nClose the cooling line before the supply. Leave occupancy until last, then pull the isolator. The plates on the manifold identify the lines.\n\nThe return drawer still catches. Put a weight on the floor release to hold it down. Don't open it while the feed is live.\n\nSomeone is walking upstairs. I came here alone. When I stop, he stops. I'm leaving my field return in the cabinet. If I don't get out, don't let them write this off as an empty house.\n\nA small stairwell key is taped to the back."
const SOURCE_COPY := "Tonight / microphone and return comparison\n\nA is the microphone: my steps through the hall. B repeats them, then adds a step I didn't take. This happened tonight. It isn't Dad's voice on an old tape.\n\nThe transport has printed the difference. I can keep this with Dad's original report. If I attach the evidence to the register, his disappearance stays open instead of being closed as an empty-house call."
const FIELD_RETURN := "Mechanical return strip / 1998\nS. Ward / arrived 23:17\nStatus changed to ABSENT / 23:18\nNo door movement. No witnessed departure.\n\nThe original notebook is in the lower drawer. Its spring release is operated from the floor.\n\nA later carbon carries tonight's work order. Restoring the carrier has brought the old call back."
const ORIGINAL := "Simon Ward / original field return / 1998\n\nThe counter keeps repeating an arrival. I disconnected the feed. The motor stopped, but the hall lights stayed on.\n\nThere is a man by the stairs. No van outside, no tools. He hasn't spoken. Every time I try to leave, he is there.\n\nI came to look at a television. Now someone has crossed my name out of the file. I'm looking at it through the office glass. I haven't left the building.\n\nPlease check the house before closing this job. Don't mark it empty on the strength of that counter.\n\nThe last page is missing. Dad pressed hard enough for his writing to mark the sheet underneath."
const RECOUNT := "Dad's original return says he was trapped inside. The office closed his call by marking him absent, without checking the house.\n\nThe porch sheet now lists his arrival beside mine. I can correct his entry and close the service call, or attach the original and the failed comparison so his disappearance stays on record. Neither choice brings him home. I still have to get the papers out of here."

static func clue(game: Node) -> String:
	if game.events.get("underfloor_read",false) and not game.events.get("line_strip_read",false) and not game.isolated and game.player.position.y>-.2 and ((game.player.position.x>1.6 and game.player.position.z< -3) or game.events.get("line_test_armed",false)):
		if game.events.get("line_response_complete",false):return "The sound came from the lounge after I disconnected the office test box. I should check what the counter did."
		if game.events.get("line_test_armed",false):return "Both leads are disconnected. Dad listened from the hall, with the lounge shut."
		return "Dad tested the timber below the office, then the continuity box upstairs. His annotation is still pinned there."
	if game.events.get("case_v3",false) and game.events.get("field_return_read",false) and not game.events.get("bedroom_left",false):
		if game.events.get("last_page_read",false):return "I have Dad's last page. I can leave the room."
		if game.events.get("receiver_found",false):return "I heard something beyond the lounge door. Dad wrote that the room changed after he shut it."
		if game.events.get("carbon_read",false):return "104.6 is a radio frequency. There is a receiver on the office desk."
		return "The torn page left impressions. The office writing mat has a soft pencil."
	if game.events.get("departure_pending","")!="":return "I have the receipt. I need to get it out to the lane."
	if game.isolated and game.events.get("case_v2",false) and not game.events.get("field_return_read",false):return "The lower return drawer needs its floor release held down. A mug is too light."
	if game.isolated:return "The original contradicts the office file. The porch register still carries the false entry."
	if game.shed_read:return "Match the circuit names in Simon's note to the plates on the relay."
	if game.report_read:return "The brass key fits the service door beside the utility bench."
	if game.stage >= 3:return "Power reached the office archive. Its date matters."
	if game.fuse:return "The kitchen carrier and the spare part share the same rating."
	if game.stage >= 1:return "The utility stock board lists a spare electrical cartridge."
	return "The paper beside the entrance explains why you were sent here."
